WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.456
An open network receives external requests,
routes them among resources and eventually

00:00:05.456 --> 00:00:11.103
releases them. A request may visit a device
repeatedly. If external arrival rate is λ and

00:00:11.103 --> 00:00:14.021
average visits are V, device throughput is λV.

00:00:14.021 --> 00:00:19.603
Multiplying by service time per visit gives
utilization. Total demand D=VS separates how

00:00:19.603 --> 00:00:22.838
often a resource is used from the cost of each
use.

00:00:23.021 --> 00:00:29.449
Under the simplified single-server station
assumptions, each device contributes D/(1−λD) to

00:00:29.449 --> 00:00:35.876
request response time. Sum these contributions
using consistent per-request accounting, and

00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:41.880
calculate average system population as λR. The
ATM example exposes nonlinear scaling:

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:48.025
doubling arrival rate increases CPU utilization
from 0.468 to 0.936 when CPU visits are

00:00:48.025 --> 00:00:48.802
twenty-six.

00:00:49.021 --> 00:00:55.332
Corrected response rises from about 0.447
seconds to 2.699 seconds, rather than simply

00:00:55.332 --> 00:01:01.936
doubling. The source arithmetic needs repair
before reuse. At two transactions/s, 4.5 disk

00:01:01.936 --> 00:01:08.173
visits per transaction and 20 ms per visit, what
are disk throughput and utilization?

00:01:08.173 --> 00:01:16.005
Disk throughput is 9 I/O/s; utilization is
9×0.02=0.18, or 18%.

00:01:16.173 --> 00:01:20.919
A closed model keeps a fixed population
circulating through the modeled workload.

00:01:20.919 --> 00:01:26.017
Interactive users alternate between thinking and
requesting service; their next request

00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:31.115
depends on completing the previous cycle. An
open model instead specifies arrivals from

00:01:31.115 --> 00:01:31.584
outside.

00:01:31.673 --> 00:01:37.161
Mixed models can contain both classes. Choosing
the workload model is a behavioral decision,

00:01:37.161 --> 00:01:40.443
not a cosmetic change in how the same diagram is
drawn.

00:01:40.673 --> 00:01:46.041
To derive a queueing model from execution
results, identify resource stations, connect
their

00:01:46.041 --> 00:01:51.408
routes, choose the workload population or
arrival rate and estimate service demand.
Preserve

00:01:51.408 --> 00:01:56.660
whether quantities are per visit or per request.
Check sensitivity to uncertain inputs and

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.585
report average-model limitations.

00:01:58.673 --> 00:02:05.117
In the authorization example, CPU demand 0.0311
seconds and utilization 0.0933 give a CPU

00:02:05.117 --> 00:02:11.705
response contribution near 0.0343 seconds,
exposing the source’s factor-of-ten error before

00:02:11.705 --> 00:02:18.294
computing the system total. Does a fixed group
of users who wait for each response generate

00:02:18.294 --> 00:02:22.348
a constant external arrival rate independently
of delay?

00:02:22.348 --> 00:02:27.739
No. Their request rate changes with response and
think times; a closed interactive model

00:02:27.739 --> 00:02:29.148
captures that coupling.

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:34.815
The processTransaction exercise combines
execution-graph analysis with resource
contention.

00:02:34.815 --> 00:02:40.221
First compute each operation’s resource demand
from its software requests and the overhead

00:02:40.221 --> 00:02:45.387
matrix. A server action, database access and
message can each consume several hardware

00:02:45.387 --> 00:02:49.651
resources, so a database operation is not merely
one unit of disk time.

00:02:49.848 --> 00:02:54.763
Reduce sequential steps and probability-weighted
alternatives to a per-request resource-

00:02:54.763 --> 00:02:55.545
demand vector.

00:02:55.545 --> 00:03:00.550
Next apply the supplied ten-jobs-per-second
workload and check every device utilization

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:05.727
before calculating delays. If any modeled
station reaches or exceeds capacity, report that

00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:10.560
the steady-state formula is inapplicable rather
than displaying a negative response.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:16.160
The extracted text includes an unfinished worked
solution and does not fully establish which

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:21.700
branch probability labels attach to which nodes.
Verify the diagram or explicitly state the

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:26.935
assumed mapping before producing numerical
answers. If the reduced disk demand is 0.12

00:03:26.935 --> 00:03:31.987
seconds/request at ten requests/s, can the
single-server stable formula be applied?

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:37.975
No. Utilization would be 1.2; the assumed single
disk station cannot sustain the offered

00:03:37.975 --> 00:03:38.580
workload.
